title: "Fixed-horizon extremes of spectrally negative Lévy processes with Poisson resetting"
type: software
authors:
  - name: Anonymous
version: 1.0.0-candidate
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23689354
date-released: 2026-10-27
repository-code: "https://github.com/ipitchford/spectrally-negative-resetting-extremes"
url: "https://evidencepress.org/releases/spectrally-negative-resetting-extremes/"
license: CC0-1.0
keywords:
  - stochastic resetting
  - spectrally negative Lévy processes
  - extremes
  - total variation
abstract: "For a stationary spectrally negative Lévy process with Poisson resetting, the joint law of the fixed-horizon maximum and the endpoint is given, as the threshold grows, by two explicit profiles (no reset: ends near the peak; reset: ends at an ordinary level) with an explicit total-variation error uniform over all endpoint sets; the conditional path law, exactness for bounded-variation inputs and random reset positions follow. For Brownian motion this supplies the constant in Remark 3 of Dębicki, Hashorva and Michna (2026) and proves their bounds strict. Unrefereed candidate. Original code is MIT-licensed; see LICENSES.md."
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Distributional and extremal behaviour of Brownian motion with exponential resetting"
